<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ActionHint's keyboard cap — app/gui/ActionHint.qml:66-85.

        implicitWidth:  Math.max(_px(24), capText.implicitWidth + 14)
        implicitHeight: _px(24)
        radius: 6                       <- NOT scaled. ActionHint writes the cap's radius as a
                                           bare 6 and lets it stay; only the SIZE token above it
                                           goes through _px(). Reproduced as written.
        color: Qt.rgba(1,1,1,0.06)      <- 6% white over whatever is behind it
        border: Theme.line, width 1

    The letter inside is ActionHint's own rule — font.pixelSize Math.max(11, size * 0.46), bold —
    which PcView sets in code because it depends on the live scale.

    ⚠️ This is the WHOLE footprint of a footer prompt's button half. The desktop has no mode in
    which the footer draws the word alone; that is what the old full-round pill on the word was
    hiding. See the note in activity_pc_view.xml.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="#0FFFFFFF" />
    <corners android:radius="6dp" />
    <stroke android:width="1dp" android:color="@color/am_line" />
</shape>
